@startuml
' Figure 20-3: the two firing paths and the fail-closed install gate. Exactly ONE path
' fires per invocation (the no-dual-path property); BOTH fire as COMMs on the SAME
' installed program. The MATCH path (default) re-matches in Rho over one spread; the
' REPLAY fallback injects the host-computed sigma, one COMM per firing, when the gate rejects.
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam defaultFontName monospaced
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #4A5568
  FontColor #1A202C
}

title Figure 20-3 — Two firing paths + fail-closed install gate\nexactly ONE path per invocation; both fire on the SAME installed program

state "report.assert_complete()" as ReportComplete #DCEEF9
state "install gate\ninstalled_program_par <latex>\to</latex> Result\n(rho_net_lower.rs:404)" as InstallGate #E2E8F0
state "choose firing path\nrho_net_match_invocation_from_dovetail_to\n(rho_invocation.rs:1765)" as ChoosePath #FDE8D5
state "MATCH path — DEFAULT\nspread + automaton re-match in Rho\n<latex>\prod_\ell \mathit{net}_\ell \parallel \mathit{spread}</latex>\nnested + multiple redexes fire" as MatchPath #C9E7D4
state "REPLAY fallback\nrho_net_replay_invocation_from_dovetail_to\n(rho_invocation.rs:1827)\nhost-<latex>\sigma</latex> replay, one COMM per firing" as ReplayPath #C6E0F5
state "observe @OUT\n(decode_reflected_term)" as Observe #FEF7E0
state "FAIL CLOSED — never silent" as FailClosed #F8D7DA

[*] --> ReportComplete : Dovetail run report
ReportComplete --> FailClosed : incomplete
ReportComplete --> InstallGate : complete
InstallGate --> FailClosed : Err\n(lowering / unmaterialized rule)
InstallGate --> ChoosePath : Ok(installed Par)
ChoosePath --> MatchPath : Ok\n(every fired rule matchable in Rho)
ChoosePath --> ReplayPath : Err\n(AC/contextual/binder/native off-machine\nOR nested-App co-install contention)
MatchPath --> Observe : COMM(s) on installed program
ReplayPath --> Observe : COMM(s) on installed program
Observe --> [*]
FailClosed --> [*]

note bottom of ReplayPath #EAF2FB
  The fallback is the proven Stage-0 host-matched <latex>\sigma</latex>-replay
  driver: correct for every input, and the ONLY residual host
  role in firing. It fires the SAME installed <latex>\sigma</latex>-receivers —
  it does not run a second Rho machine.
end note
@enduml
